WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.830
You're coding a game
of noughts and crosses.

2
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.310
Your first try gives every
square its own variable:

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.250
square 1, square 2, all
the way to square 9.

4
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:15.210
Every move and every win check now
means juggling nine different names.

5
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:19.270
Is there a way to keep all 9
squares under just one name?

6
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.630
In this mission, you'll meet a data
structure that stores many values under one

7
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:24.890
identifier.

8
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.970
You'll pick out any one
value by its position number,

9
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.410
called its index.

10
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.990
And you'll see how each value
is found by its position.

11
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.210
Your mission: work out how one name can
hold all 9 squares of a noughts and crosses

12
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:38.720
board.
